# Self-Review Loop After Making Changes

After implementing any non-trivial code change, enter a review-fix loop:

1. Review your work with the scrutiny of a senior engineer
2. If issues are found, fix them and go back to step 1
3. Repeat until the review surfaces no new issues

Apply this scrutiny at each pass:

- Correctness: edge cases, race conditions, error paths
- Signal/process semantics, exit codes, resource cleanup
- Whether the change is complete end-to-end (e.g. config wired up, not just written)
- Coordination dependencies (does this require another change to take effect?)

If a potential fix involves a genuine trade-off (complexity vs. correctness, etc.), do not make it — describe the trade-off and let the user decide.
